  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) achieved 0.706 accuracy, dramatically outperforming image-only config_008 (0.332), confirming multimodal fusion with these encoders is the right direction. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the avgpool aggregation is optimal or whether a transformer-based aggregation could better capture cross-modal interactions between the RNA and image features. This experiment (config_012) makes a single-variable change—swapping avgpool for transformer aggregation—while holding all other components (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion, multiprofile) identical to the best config. This isolates the effect of aggregation architecture. It is the best use of experiment 3 because it directly tests the most impactful architectural upgrade available within the current best configuration, and a positive result would open a productive exploitation path for the remaining 7 experiments, while a negative result would confirm avgpool suffices and redirect effort toward other variables (RNA encoder, fusion method, image encoder)."
